<?xml version="1.0" encoding="us-ascii"?>
<XML ID="EQInterfaceDefinitionLanguage">
<!-- ============================================================================================
     AoTv4 Fellowship window.

     GENERATED BY TRANSFORMING THE CLIENT'S OWN EQUI_FellowshipWnd.xml: every coordinate, size and
     template is byte for byte the native window's, with the screen renamed AoTFellowshipWnd and
     every piece prefixed AFW_ so it cannot collide with the client's own screen. That is why it
     looks identical rather than merely similar.

     WHY WE DO NOT JUST USE THE NATIVE WINDOW: the client has it, but server side
     OP_FellowshipUpdate is a NAME IN emu_oplist.h AND NOTHING ELSE, with no handler, no struct in
     eq_packet_structs.h, and no mapping in the RoF2 patch, so it has no wire opcode for this
     client. It would open empty forever. CLAUDE.md section 13 records the same dead end for the
     native trader window.

     Driven by core_fellowship.cpp over the chat protocol, like every other AoTv4 window.
     ============================================================================================ -->
